# Artifact Sync (required, automatic)

Every non-trivial change MUST update the full sync surface in the **same** change and **same turn**. Incomplete sync = not done.

## Do not ask

- **Never** ask the user whether to update specs, docs, tests, skills, rules, or agents.
- **Never** end with “I can update the docs/tests if you want.”
- Just update them as part of the work. Silence on sync means it is done.

## Sync matrix

| If you change… | Also update… |
|----------------|--------------|
| Behavior / UX / RPC / RLS | `openspec/specs/` (or active change + archive) |
| Routes, ops, architecture | Matching `docs/**` (spec, ops, playbook, navigation) |
| Feature / bugfix | Tests (`regression_*` for bugs) per `tests-required` |
| Recurring convention | `.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md` and/or `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| Role scope / escalation | `.cursor/agents/*.md` + root `AGENTS.md` |
| Pre-push / CI gates | `.githooks/`, `.cursor/hooks/gate-git-push.sh`, `scripts/ci-local.mjs`, `edunudg-pre-push-ci`, `git-publish-gate` |

## Exempt (note in commit/PR if skipping OpenSpec)

Typos, pure refactors with zero behavior change, dependency bumps only.

## Before finishing

1. Run skill `edunudg-sync-artifacts` checklist (proactively)
2. Confirm Definition of Done sync section
3. Do **not** leave “docs/tests later” TODOs for sync items
